differs by one `payloadEnumNames.get` I cannot locate — I count 5, they
report 6; the inventory below is exhaustive under the command above, so if
their 33rd exists it is outside these five files).

Meaning of the keys:
- `exceptionPayloads`: class MODULE → payload-enum module. **Class identity is
  the meaning**; a collision (two exception classes in one Haxe module) mistypes
  one of them.
- `payloadEnumNames` / `payloadEnumOwners`: payload-enum MODULE → enum name /
  owning class name. Enum-identity-by-module; collides only if **two payload
  enums share one module** (a different axis, see §5).
- `payloadEnumModules`: payload-enum MODULE → emitted module path. Emission
  location is genuinely a *module* property, so module keying is the intended
  semantics.

