## 3. The change (PATCH.diff, 4 sites, +35/−8 lines)

Each change is the same minimal shape: consult
`state.exceptionPayloadEnums.get(module + "::" + name)` (the class-keyed map
the earlier fix already maintains) **first**, falling back to the old
module-keyed lookup when no class-keyed entry exists. When both exist they
agree by construction (the `set` site writes both from the same pair), so
single-class-per-module shapes generate byte-identical code — confirmed in §4.

1. `RustExpr.hx` `catchPayloadAccess` — the counterexample site.
2. `Compiler.hx` `caughtPayloadEnumModuleOf` — reviewer nomination.
3. `RustDecl.hx` `caughtPayloadEnumModuleOf` — reviewer nomination.
4. `RustType.hx` exception-type import path — same axis, not previously
   nominated.

PATCH.diff applies cleanly to the audited earlier-fix state (round-trip
verified: apply → byte-identical to the post tree, then revert → audited
hashes back).

